        "ephanna"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 1.0,
      "failure_surface": "synthesis_gap",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "bonogo": "evidence_gap",
        "caelynn": "evidence_gap",
        "thalia": "hit",
        "wolf": "hit",
        "guards": "hit",
        "ephanna": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The chamber contains the Players, the Wolf, Thalia, and multiple Guards (including elite and possibly corrupted ones); no council members are explicitly confirmed present in the provided context.\n\nBased on OBSERVED and CANON facts tied to the Session 12 confrontation:\n\n- **Players (group)** \u2014 actively involved in the fight and previously recounting events to the council, placing them in the chamber.\n- **the Wolf** \u2014 explicitly identified as the central adversary \u201cin the council chamber battle.\u201d\n- **Thalia (Commander of the Guard)** \u2014 present with \u201cWolf is standing at Thalia\u2019s shoulder\u201d and participates in combat after his command.\n- **Guards** \u2014 present in force:\n  - Reinforcements are \u201cbeing drawn here as reinforcements\u201d (CANON, Council Chambers).\n  - Guards are \u201cactively stopping people outside Council Chambers\u201d and some engage directly in combat.\n  - Composition includes \u201c8 regular guards\u2026 and 2 elite guards,\u201d with some corrupted (OBSERVED).\n\nNotably absent:\n- **Council members** are not explicitly confirmed as present during the fight in this projection, despite the location.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- **Participants:** Players, the Wolf, Thalia, Guards (regular + elite, some corrupted)\n- **Combat context:** Active battle with reinforcements arriving\n- **Environment:** Council chamber with magical defenses (illusory walls, runes) and a hidden trapdoor\n- **Tension factors:** Corruption (oily sheen), divided guard loyalty, Thalia ensorcelled",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_longmont_campaign_general_notes_1",
      "question": "Who are the Shepherds, and what god or power do they answer to?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "semantic_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "must_hits": [
        "shepherds",
