        "detect",
        "counter corruption"
      ],
      "context_must_hits": [
        "headmaster tinkerbright",
        "wizard's college",
        "detect",
        "counter corruption"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 1.0,
      "failure_surface": "pass",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "headmaster tinkerbright": "hit",
        "wizard's college": "hit",
        "detect": "hit",
        "counter corruption": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright speaks for the wizards; he treats the cult as a dangerous perversion of magic and pushes aggressive arcane solutions like detection spells and a citywide magical lockdown.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright (gnome, Head of the Wizard\u2019s College) is the council\u2019s arcane representative. [OBSERVED/CANON] His role is explicitly \u201cRepresentative of the Arcane\u201d and he leads the Wizard\u2019s College.\n\nHis angle on the cult is strongly interventionist and magic-focused:\n- He views the corrupted meat as \u201ca perversion of magic\u201d and takes the threat very seriously. [CANON]\n- He is eager to deploy Wizard\u2019s College resources to detect and counteract the cult\u2019s influence. [OBSERVED]\n- He plans to use a rune-based method to locate corrupted meat and supports a potential magical lockdown of the city. [OBSERVED]\n- On persuasion, he offers the Wizards\u2019 College detection spell to aid investigations. [CANON]\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Head of the Wizard\u2019s College; Representative of the Arcane  \n- Alignment toward cult: Urgent, anti-cult, sees it as magical corruption  \n- Strategy: Detection magic, resource deployment, possible arcane lockdown  \n- Personality: Brilliant, curious, but easily distracted by experiments",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
