      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Merril handles food and agriculture, Torrin represents the craft guilds, and Rurik oversees infrastructure and the city\u2019s structural integrity.\n\nMerril Tealeaf  \n- Role: Representative of Agriculture and Food Production (CANON)  \n- Title: Leader of the Agricultural Union (OBSERVED)  \n- Function on council: Advocates for food safety, agriculture, and public well-being\u2014especially pushing to cleanse contaminated supplies.\n\nTorrin Flamescale  \n- Role: Representative of the Craft Guilds / Master Smith (OBSERVED)  \n- Faction: the Guilds (CANON)  \n- Function on council: Speaks for artisans and industry; provides practical, blunt input on city matters affecting production and trade.\n\nRurik Stonehammer  \n- Role: Representative of Infrastructure (CANON)  \n- Title: Chief Architect (OBSERVED)  \n- Function on council: Responsible for the city\u2019s structural integrity, defenses, and layout\u2014especially tunnels, sewers, and sealing threats.\n\nKey Attributes:  \n- Governance: Each is a council representative tied to a civic domain (agriculture, guilds, infrastructure).  \n- Responsibilities: Food safety (Merril), industry/crafts (Torrin), city structure/defenses (Rurik).",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_1",
      "question": "When the council-chamber fight ends, where does that leave the Wolf-dead, fled, what?",
