      "context_support_ratio": 1.0,
      "failure_surface": "pass",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "killed": "hit",
        "killing blow": "hit",
        "bonogo": "hit",
        "decapitated": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight **dead** \u2014 specifically **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** \u2014 with Bonogo taking the head.\n\nThe projection shows conflicting mid-fight possibilities (invisibility and escape), but the **latest OBSERVED outcomes** resolve it:  \n- The Wolf had been **\u201cDisappeared (became invisible)\u201d** and attempting escape via the secret passage (OBSERVED operational_status).  \n- However, this is superseded by later OBSERVED facts: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (physical_condition) and Bonogo **\u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it\u201d** (role).\n\nBecause decapitation is a terminal outcome, it definitively overrides the earlier escape attempt. The Wolf is not fled or missing\u2014he is dead.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Status: **Dead \u2014 \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (OBSERVED)\n- Last actions: Attempted escape while invisible via secret passage (OBSERVED, superseded)\n- Killer/aftermath: Bonogo removed and took the head (OBSERVED)\n- Role: Council chamber saboteur and central adversary (CANON)\n\nNet: the fight concludes with the Wolf eliminated, body destroyed, and head in party possession.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
