      "answer": "TL;DR: The projection does not state that Thalia is corrupted like the guards; her behavior appears driven by The Wolf\u2019s influence, but the exact nature (corruption vs. control) is not specified.\n\nBased on the available facts:\n- **Guards** are explicitly corrupted, shown by \u201can oily sheen to their eyes\u201d and mutations/interaction with corrupted meat.\n- **The Wolf** also shows corruption markers (\u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d) and actively **orders Thalia to attack the group**.\n- **Thalia** herself has no listed physical condition or corruption markers in the projection.\n\nThis suggests a distinction: Thalia\u2019s aggression is clearly linked to **The Wolf\u2019s command**, but there is no evidence she shares the guards\u2019 confirmed corruption traits. Without explicit mention (like the oily sheen or physical transformation), her state remains **unclear\u2014possibly influence, coercion, or manipulation rather than full corruption**.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Guards: corrupted (oily sheen, mutation, meat interaction)\n- The Wolf: corrupting influence; oily sheen; directs Thalia\n- Thalia: no confirmed corruption markers; acts under The Wolf\u2019s orders",
      "embedding_similarity": null
