      "answer": "TL;DR: The council room interferes via arcane trap bursts, unstable structure (falling debris), and disorienting magical effects like illusion and sensory cues.\n\n**Hazards in the council room (grounded):**\n- **Arcane trap bursts** (CANON/OBSERVED via Players physical_condition): deal *2d6 force damage* and can *temporarily paralyze* targets; may preferentially target those without amulets (Players defenses).\n- **Falling debris** (OBSERVED): structural instability forces players to dodge hazards; can knock them **prone**.\n- **Illusory distortions** (CANON): players are *disoriented by illusory walls/illusion spells*, interfering with movement and targeting.\n- **Sensory disruption** (CANON portrayal_notes + city portrayal): shifting **hum** in the environment signals changes, potentially masking danger or triggering effects mid-fight.\n- **Reinforcement pressure cues** (CANON): **echoing footsteps** suggest incoming threats, adding urgency and distraction even if not immediately visible.\n\n**Key Attributes:**\n- Defenses: Arcane traps tied to amulet protection.\n- Environment: Structurally unstable (debris) and magically active (illusions, ambient hum).\n- Player Impact: Prone, paralyzed, disoriented, and pressured by perceived reinforcements.",
