      "answer": "TL;DR: There isn\u2019t enough evidence to say Thalia is untrustworthy, but there are indirect signs that something around her may be off.\n\nBased on the projection, Thalia has very little direct characterization. However, a few OBSERVED facts create uncertainty:\n\n- Stafl \u201cAttacks Thalia after being revived,\u201d which suggests either suspicion, confusion, or altered judgment on Stafl\u2019s part.\n- Caelynn is \u201cTalking with Thalia about the plans\u201d and \u201cInstructs Thalia to bring a potion to Lesandra at the Wizard\u2019s College,\u201d indicating Thalia is being trusted with important tasks by at least one party member.\n\nThere are no explicit signs of corruption, deception, or altered mental state tied to Thalia (unlike the Guards, who show \u201can oily sheen to their eyes\u201d).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Relationships: Trusted by Caelynn for mission tasks (OBSERVED)\n- Threat indicators: Targeted by Stafl\u2019s attack (OBSERVED)\n- Corruption markers: None stated\n\nConclusion: No hard evidence against Thalia, but the situation around her (especially Stafl\u2019s behavior) justifies caution.",
