      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Delay lets the cult advance its summoning, exploit hidden routes, and potentially corrupt the city from within while defenses remain uncertain\u2014escalating toward a citywide disaster.\n\nIf the council stalls, the biggest consequences are already in motion:\n\n- Cult progress: The cult is \u201cattempting to summon the flesh kaiju\u201d and \u201ccomplete their summoning\u201d (CANON: the cult goals). Time directly benefits them.\n- Infiltration advantage: They are \u201cusing hidden routes\u201d and \u201crely on the sewers\u201d (CANON: the cult current_location, relationship_tags), so inaction gives them freedom to reposition or bypass any delayed response.\n- Sabotage risk: They \u201ccould sabotage or corrupt the cauldrons\u201d (CANON: the cult goals), worsening the tainted meat crisis the council is debating.\n- Internal compromise: \u201cCult members have influence in the council\u201d (CANON: the cult relationship_tags), meaning continued debate may actively serve the enemy.\n- City destabilization: The city is already \u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate\u201d and \u201cits stability and well-being are threatened by the cult\u201d (OBSERVED: the city operational_status).\n- Defense failure: The city\u2019s defenses have \u201cintegrity\u2026 a matter of concern\u201d and a \u201cplanned magical lockdown\u201d is not yet enacted (CANON/OBSERVED: the city defenses, operational_status).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Threat: The cult (summoning, infiltration, sabotage, council influence)\n- City Status: Unstable, delayed decision-making, threatened defenses\n- Geography: Hidden passages/sewers enable enemy movement\n- Governance: Council gridlock worsens outcomes",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
