      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room is tense and visibly corrupted\u2014The Wolf is **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, and multiple guards show the same unsettling **oily sheen to their eyes**, signaling the deeper threat still present.\n\nWhat you should notice (grounded):\n\n- The Wolf: His body is down and definitively ended\u2014**\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (OBSERVED, the Wolf physical_condition). If the head was taken (Bonogo), that absence is also noticeable.\n- Corruption signs: Both The Wolf and guards share **\u201can oily sheen to their eyes\u201d** (OBSERVED, the Wolf physical_condition; Guards physical_condition), reinforcing the cult\u2019s influence.\n- Guards\u2019 state: Surviving guards are **visibly tense**, possibly shaken or in disbelief (OBSERVED, Guards mental_state), and some may still be compromised.\n- Formation/positioning: Guards were **placed in a ring along the wall** (OBSERVED, Guards current_location), suggesting a defensive lockdown posture during or after the fight.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Guards may still be influenced by corruption mechanics tied to meat (CANON).\n- Operational Status: Guards were actively responding to alarms and threats near the Council Chamber (OBSERVED).\n- Atmosphere: Tension, uncertainty, and lingering threat from infiltration/corruption.",
