      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead at the end of Session 12\u2014**\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** He showed signs of corruption (oily sheen eyes) up to that point, with no evidence it was cured before death.\n\n**What\u2019s current vs earlier:**\n- OBSERVED earlier: The Wolf was **Invisible**, escaping via secret passage and evading pursuit.\n- OBSERVED later (terminal outcome): **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** Bonogo also **\u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d**\n- The terminal outcome overrides prior escape states\u2014he is definitively dead by session end.\n\n**Corruption state:**\n- OBSERVED: **\u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d** (marker of corruption)\n- No OBSERVED resolution (no cleansing or \u201ceyes fade\u201d), so he dies still corrupted.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Enemy; saboteur; central adversary in council chamber battle\n- Faction: cultist\n- Rank: second-in-command of the guard\n- Abilities: creates illusory duplicates; uses invisibility\n- Mental state: desperate, regretful, begging for release / death\n- Physical condition (final): **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**",
      "embedding_similarity": null
