      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive saboteur manipulating events; after, he\u2019s a broken, exposed cultist who is **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** and no longer a threat.\n\nBefore the fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is a **second-in-command of the guard** and covert **cultist/saboteur**.\n- Actively manipulates the council via **Deception/Persuasion** and misdirection.\n- Uses **illusory duplicates** and confusion tactics.\n- Operationally dangerous: **turns invisible, attempts escape via secret tunnel**, directs allies (e.g., orders Thalia to attack).\n- Composed and strategic, though aware of danger.\n\nAfter the fight (OBSERVED):\n- Physically defeated: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**\n- Prior to death shows a sharp mental shift: **begging to be killed, desperate, regretful**.\n- His corruption is more apparent (**oily sheen to his eyes**).\n- No longer an active manipulator or escape threat.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Enemy saboteur \u2192 Neutralized target\n- Mental State: Calculating \u2192 Desperate, regretful\n- Physical Condition: Mobile/invisible \u2192 **Decapitated; head removed from body**\n- Tactics: Illusions, deception \u2192 None (terminated)\n- Allegiance: Hidden cultist \u2192 Exposed cultist",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_thalia",
      "question": "Was Thalia corrupted or just played-and how does that tie to the Wolf?",
