        "not corrupted": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was **not corrupted** in the same way as others\u2014she was **ensorcelled by the Wolf (i.e., magically manipulated/\u201cplayed\u201d)**, not willingly turned or physically corrupted.\n\n**What the projection supports:**\n\n- **OBSERVED (Thalia physical_condition):** \u201cThalia does not have an oily sheen to her eyes\u201d and is explicitly \u201censorcelled\u2026 by the Wolf.\u201d\n- **OBSERVED (contrast with Guards):** Corrupted individuals consistently show \u201can oily sheen to their eyes,\u201d which Thalia lacks.\n- **OBSERVED (Thalia mental_state):** She is described as \u201cInnocent,\u201d with her \u201cCharmed status ended\u201d and later \u201cRealizes how dire the situation truly is.\u201d\n- **OBSERVED (Wolf influence):** \u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d and is physically positioned (\u201cWolf is standing at Thalia\u2019s shoulder.\u201d)\n\n**Interpretation grounded in facts:**\nThalia wasn\u2019t a true convert or corrupted agent\u2014she was **under magical control or influence (ensorcellment)**. That\u2019s why she could:\n- Act against the party under the Wolf\u2019s command\n- Be **convinced of the Wolf\u2019s betrayal** afterward\n- Return to clearer judgment once the charm ended\n\n**Key Attributes**\n- Physical Condition: Ensorcelled; no oily sheen (not corrupted)\n- Mental State: Innocent; charmed \u2192 recovered awareness\n- Loyalty Context: Serves the Wolf (under influence), but protective of the city\n- Wolf Tie: Direct magical control and command authority over her actions",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    }
